# The Red Hand's toll (docs/ERRANDS.md, "Duties"; Missions/Errands/RZ_DutyRedHand.c, Toll): whoever
# comes to the pole stands there to be talked to (RZ_TalkDutyPerson). The working conversation is
# shared (duty.toll.pole): asking where they're bound is the beat's option 2 (one of its two looks),
# and the three calls are options 3 take the toll, 4 wave them through, 5 turn them back. Some have a
# word of their own besides (who they are), which settles nothing.

conv duty.toll.pole
for duty:toll
topic "Stop there. Toll."
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say? night :: They stop where the lamp reaches, no closer, and wait to hear what it costs.
  say They stop at the pole, and wait to hear what it costs.
  > @bound Where are you bound? -> heard   do call:slot:2
  > @call Right. Here's how it goes. -> call

node heard
  say They answer, and watch your hands while they do it.
  > @call2 Right. Here's how it goes. -> call

node call
  say The pole stays down until you say.
  > @take Toll's paid here. Hand it over. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @wave Go on through. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @turn Not today. Back the way you came. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.toll.handcart
for duty:toll:handcart
topic "How old are the little ones?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Four and six. They walked the first day and then they stopped walking, and now they sleep. I envy them. I've not slept since the roads shut.
  > @back0 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.courier
for duty:toll:courier
topic "What's in the satchel?"
prio flavour
once
voice haven

node start
  say Letters, mostly. A dressing or two. The Haven sends a runner to the farms on this road every third day, and the farms send eggs back. Ask anyone. It's not a secret.
  > @back1 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.deserter
for duty:toll:deserter
topic "That's Bastion kit."
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say It was. I've taken the patches off. They sent us to hold a bridge with nine rounds each, and I counted the rounds and counted the dead, and I walked.
  > @back2 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.tech
for duty:toll:tech
topic "What's in the case?"
prio flavour
once
voice halcyon

node start
  say Samples. Sealed for your protection and mine. I'm not authorised to open it, and if I were, I'd advise you to stand well back.
  > @back3 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.child
for duty:toll:child
topic "Where are your people?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say My aunt's in the next town. She has a blue door. I know the way. I've been once, before, in a car. It was quicker in a car.
  > @back4 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.oldman
for duty:toll:oldman
topic "What have you got for me?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Nothing but news, son. And the news is this: the ferry man at the river has stopped taking bread. He takes boots now. Remember that one. It's worth a toll.
  > @back5 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.bitten
for duty:toll:bitten
topic "Why the long sleeves?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Cold. It's cold. Everybody's cold. I just want to get to my sister's, that's all, she has a stove.
  > @back6 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.runner
for duty:toll:runner
topic "Whose crew are you with?"
prio flavour
once
voice redhand

node start
  say Same as you, mate, just a different boss. Mine says yours owes him for a crate. I'm not carrying that message. I'm carrying this one, and it's not for you.
  > @back7 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.priest
for duty:toll:priest
topic "Where's your parish, Father?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Wherever they still bury people properly. It's a moving parish these days. I'll say a word for your lot too, if you let me through. Even for your lot.
  > @back8 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.widow
for duty:toll:widow
topic "Who are you in black for?"
prio flavour
once
voice haven

node start
  say My husband. He was on this road with the cart, the first week. I've come to see the place. That's all. I won't stay long. I just want to see the place.
  > @back9 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.pedlar
for duty:toll:pedlar
topic "What are you selling?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Needles, thread, buttons, bootlaces, a lucky rabbit's foot, unlucky for the rabbit. Everything a man forgets he needs until he needs it. Discount for the pole.
  > @back10 Right. -> hub

conv duty.toll.hunter
for duty:toll:hunter
topic "Good hunting up there?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

node start
  say Deer's come down out of the high woods. Nobody's shooting them now, so they've stopped being afraid of a man walking. They're still afraid of the other things.
  > @back11 Right. -> hub
